nited States Army general during World War II?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"George S. Patton led the Third Army after the Normandy invasion, and his forces helped liberate much of France.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c1e-b03c-7afc03956ed0","description":"George S. Patton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-79b1-80c0-cfd921739419","description":"David Dixon Porter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-790a-9042-bd2b3337d8ba","description":"George Elliot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-75f8-8c72-26f2e81f1aaa","description":"Philip Sheridan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-740f-a366-94ac4ac25f05","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the American Civil War end?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Civil War ended in 1865; Lee\'s surrender at Appomattox Court House in April marked a decisive turning point, though fighting continued briefly elsewhere.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7334-9691-eaadeccf568e","description":"1865","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-747b-8f27-6410f9727007","description":"1863","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7682-b3f8-63255ee4364b","description":"1861","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7e7c-ab3f-ed4a69e9019e","description":"1877","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7e32-9716-0f915601b940","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Betrayed by a fellow gang member, which Wild West outlaw was shot dead in 1882 while dusting a picture frame?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Jesse James was already a notorious post-Civil War outlaw when Robert Ford shot him, hoping to collect a reward.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7fe0-a429-9d695329dc5e","description":"Jesse James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7995-ab9f-4172ab52c7e1","description":"Billy the Kid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7f9f-88af-63e55ff8032c","description":"Butch Cassidy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-78a7-8b7a-51e6653f9d73","description":"John Wesley Hardin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-79dc-8fe0-0ed757919576","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the European Union (EU) form?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Maastricht Treaty was signed in 1992 and brought the European Union into existence when it took effect the following year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-71c6-8154-38b951d154d8","description":"1993","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c60-bf82-6cfcfa297c12","description":"1973","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-785c-94f7-c707aa86c841","description":"1953","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-70db-9bbf-ace2c310e477","description":"1933","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7a95-b9e3-4b4b22369a63","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"As what is the Frankish ruler Charles the Great better known?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Charlemagne united much of western and central Europe, and his reign helped foster the Carolingian Renaissance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-71cc-9b53-92382140b9f7","description":"Charlemagne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7b78-94f1-8a324f14ea46","description":"Charles the Bald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-777a-91d9-671474b691fa","description":"Charlione","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d44-9d10-e8e65ff92532","description":"Charity Charles","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d26-8600-4a071793e84a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What explorer landed in China and reached Kublai Khan\'s court in 1275?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Marco Polo\'s travels, reaching Kublai Khan\'s court around 1275, were recorded in The Travels of Marco Polo.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-70a7-8b90-532d5f9247df","description":"Marco Polo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-789d-a5bc-1b575484