","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c80-a24d-c6a74f359f26","description":"Harold Wilson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-78d6-a514-3aa39a75e710","description":"Tony Blair","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-72b2-b9e8-82b604d62314","description":"John Major","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7e0e-8aa0-9a8fd4dcf4bc","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which US election year were the supporters of the Democratic candidate paraphrasing the popular song \"Hello Dolly\" to \"Hello Lyndon\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In 1964, Lyndon B. Johnson won a full term after succeeding Kennedy, defeating Republican Barry Goldwater in a landslide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7612-a548-7f77c82c73c6","description":"1964","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-718d-9fb6-cad38bdfa369","description":"1944","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c3c-a653-dc37a0fe0c76","description":"1980","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7b2a-816e-d3f228894154","description":"1992","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c66-84bd-337e2fb3839a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the monarch of The United Kingdom during the time period 1837-1901?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Victoria was the first British monarch to make Buckingham Palace her official residence.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7e1e-be6c-e2b9b50c1db2","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-75e8-b978-460a2ac8bf74","description":"Mary II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-74a6-a622-6db2e774216b","description":"Richard I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7ae6-aefb-24530a30ccd8","description":"William IV","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-717c-9d85-34315aad63b2","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Church body, set up in the 13th century to root out heresy, became known for its trials and torture?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The medieval Inquisition was a series of church tribunals. The Spanish Inquisition, established later, became especially notorious, though it was a distinct institution.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-788e-9f69-3120ba528667","description":"The Inquisition","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-77ba-a943-062e1da4abc5","description":"The Knights Templar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-749d-8ff7-a2762e47722d","description":"The Curia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7a3f-9d84-5a5d5c4aeb10","description":"The Jesuits","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7b25-a59e-78efa95f60b9","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The eldest sons of the kings of which country held the title \'Dauphin\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The title came from the Dauphin\u00e9, a region that became part of the royal domain; it was later used for the heir to the French throne.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-76b5-b05c-4effe405fe7d","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-70b2-b944-8c750d96e7f7","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-794c-b1e0-277d07b0cfde","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-77da-ac5a-b91afb9f3c50","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-77eb-a170-d811fa7ed7bf","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Founded in 1636, what is the oldest university in the USA?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Harvard was named for John Harvard, a clergyman whose bequest of books and money helped the young college grow.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c4d-ae2a-860368ed99ed","description":"Harvard","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-70ba-8aa9-1a2542dd2ce5","description":"Stanford","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-756e-8e00-62bd12927b36","description":"Cornell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d36-9557-18