ipher Egyptian hieroglyphs.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-753f-bd00-228657986a31","description":"The Rosetta Stone","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-768f-aa6c-d7140c24938d","description":"The Philosopher\'s Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d55-b084-7e6407fa7f3d","description":"The Stone of Destiny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7620-805c-cc0e4cd9810d","description":"The Cornerstone","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d68-a4ba-bf32a021af18","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which British general commanded the army that surrendered at Yorktown in the American Revolution?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"American and French forces surrounded Charles Cornwallis at Yorktown, while the French navy blocked British relief, forcing his surrender.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-79f9-bfe3-8b2bf8785a00","description":"Charles Cornwallis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7caa-ada4-2bb0d3beaa48","description":"John Burgoyne","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7004-ac25-a35f942156b5","description":"William Howe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-71d4-b13b-fcc44d5d8b7e","description":"Henry Clinton","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7020-9c19-cb674eba5183","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese emperor was buried with an army of thousands of life-sized clay soldiers?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Qin Shi Huang unified China and founded the Qin dynasty. His burial complex includes the terracotta army, intended to guard him in the afterlife.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-75bb-9c68-cc1d58a76bb1","description":"Qin Shi Huang","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-767c-8916-630312c3c09a","description":"Han Wudi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c4b-8271-b14db4c57aa7","description":"Kangxi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-73e9-a982-f62bf9982978","description":"Yongle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7425-9ee5-b0252085b4c9","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Battles known as Con Thien and Hamburger Hill were fought during which 20th century conflict?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Vietnam refers to the Vietnam War, in which the United States fought alongside South Vietnam against North Vietnam and its allies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7e84-9922-4d7392d06f44","description":"Vietnam","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7c7d-8207-6fd99fe9e22f","description":"Iraq","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-76cc-9de5-95d1d6a33c31","description":"Korea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7bfb-a32d-ad939e213877","description":"Afghanistan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-72dc-8cf7-7b76ea1453d5","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did Neil Armstrong first step onto the Moon?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Armstrong stepped onto the lunar surface after the Apollo 11 spacecraft Eagle landed; Buzz Aldrin followed him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-750e-9a7c-6226da0f6dbc","description":"1969","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d65-9c80-fbceacc1bf20","description":"1967","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7d64-aac4-75e626640fca","description":"1971","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-73e3-9ba7-54103d59608d","description":"1973","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7b67-8027-acdf7ad1791a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year was Hong Kong Island formally ceded to Britain under the Treaty of Nanking?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Britain occupied the island in 1841, and it was ceded by the Treaty of Nanking signed in 1842 after the First Opium War.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7312-9c4f-1e7e74283c5e","description":"1842","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-79a8-a10a-ca7c6f26f1a2","description":"1815","correct_answe