":"Anne Boleyn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7fd7-9168-00553d0d5cfa","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-716a-b237-d5a538ebfe3d","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Russian city was known as Leningrad between 1924 and 1991?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"St Petersburg was renamed Petrograd in 1914 and Leningrad in 1924; the city restored its original name in 1991.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7351-acba-8ce0c3338639","description":"St Petersburg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7cc2-95e9-ee3dbba666fd","description":"Kazan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7762-a51e-f666773a364f","description":"Nizhny Novgorod","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7df5-ad47-6798ce6051b6","description":"Moscow","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7190-b42d-851212ff58bc","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What ancient civilization occupied the city of Cusco?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Inca made Cusco the capital of their empire, which extended across much of the Andes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7f71-bacc-52f6b9a00584","description":"The Inca","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-78d1-96e3-cb24b147129d","description":"The Aztecs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7f2a-af3f-61774d7ec0bd","description":"The Mayans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7533-8d84-964c27a5bcb7","description":"The Zapotecs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-753f-a118-9f9c04732515","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What were the first names of US presidents Madison, Monroe, Polk, and Garfield?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"James Madison and James Monroe served as consecutive presidents, with Monroe following Madison.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7bc5-adc5-717f35c928a8","description":"James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad30-7262-af21-ae869e680ae0"