:false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7de5-a67d-16d09fa1ae82","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What year did World War II begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1939 is the year Germany invaded Poland on September 1; Britain and France declared war two days later.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7d93-bb23-ce16b73963f2","description":"1939","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7cf9-ac02-cb31ad4d3153","description":"1941","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7aae-b254-1155b0f8a811","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-76b9-8038-f140d7665ad8","description":"1937","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-76a7-b79b-0f22dd401e48","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which World War I battle is remembered for the Parisian taxicabs that ferried French troops to the front line in 1914?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The French victory at the Marne halted the German advance toward Paris and helped set the Western Front into a prolonged stalemate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7f3d-b860-9fd446f37861","description":"Battle of the Marne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-78b1-bfb8-113d6b179d6a","description":"Battle of the Somme","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7e5e-a52e-fc8c565a2c2b","description":"Battle of Ypres","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-771a-9ac4-76c08e0fa5fb","description":"Battle of Verdun","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7967-91c9-846b8af1eae5","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the major economic revolution that started in the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain and reshaped manufacturing as production shifted toward machinery and factories.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-720c-a003-48b9c2738446","description":"The Industrial Revolution","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7b6b-8a36-b04c4565bd47","description":"The French Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7d47-ba80-573f83317d9d","description":"The American Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7342-ba3b-8afbd2cc9e0f","description":"The Enlightenment","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7bbb-b7c3-99eb0984749c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What group of ships, commanded by the Duke of Medina, was considered invincible but was defeated by The Royal Navy in 1588?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Spanish Armada was disrupted by English fireships, and storms battered many ships as they retreated around Scotland and Ireland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7804-ae11-3423ac7986cd","description":"Spanish Armada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7416-b316-a6d1951ea896","description":"The Napoleonic Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7744-a885-83b8498c1c34","description":"The Viking Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-73eb-b7c7-329f2b67af5c","description":"The Scottish Armada","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-796c-8de3-91b3a069a7f6","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the second man to walk on the Moon, after Neil Armstrong?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Buzz Aldrin and Neil Armstrong landed together while Michael Collins remained aboard the command module in lunar orbit.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7323-a2fe-16c37ea69516","description":"Buzz Aldrin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7a64-b645-512d72c62dea","description":"Yuri Gagarin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7ac8-86c1-88fc838633c3","description":"Alan Shepard","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-793e-8952-faa5966fd0d4","description":"James Irwin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7eba-a05e-672cef6370ca","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What kind of government dominated most of Europe during the 17th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Absolute monarchs centralized authority over government, taxation, and the military. Louis XIV of France is one of the best-known examples.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7208-8539-d6a306f7ddec","description":"Absolute Monarchy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-754c-90ea-1c7379b48069","description":"Democracy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7447-860e-3e5b10bcc17e","description":"Constitutional Monarchy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-749c-a12e-7db5e85cdf94","description":"Parliamentary Democracy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7553-a053-4cb0a98b7f75","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What city was destroyed by a \'little boy\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hiroshima was struck by the first atomic bomb used in warfare, dropped by the U.S. B-29 Enola Gay in August 1945.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-75e7-8887-26b6e1cd9a0a","description":"Hiroshima","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7d16-8a30-7b30fa45a88e","description":"Jericho","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7461-8d9c-4f89ac046104","description":"Babel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7b55-89a8-16ff0a1904a1","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-75fb-9734-b8af08a5aeba","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What age preceded the Iron Age?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, and its widespread use gave this period its name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7bd7-9668-a607c42745be","description":"The Bronze Age","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7030-ba6f-ddb756400249","description":"The Stone Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7bd3-acc9-dbcefc30e4f2","description":"The Steel Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7f29-9eff-8f5861da805b","description":"The Wooden Age","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-77da-b7c2-8076b27ffa9d","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What notorious event occurred on the 24th October 1929?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Wall Street Crash began with Black Thursday, as investors rushed to sell shares. The market turmoil helped usher in the Great Depression.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7503-a5a5-4d2272f5f7c9","description":"The Wall Street Crash","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-723a-9ac8-230351948966","description":"The Hindenberg Disaster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7343-a42f-b79694821748","description":"The Assassination of John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7773-8fc5-a13050d55017","description":"The Nazi Invasion of Poland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-760a-97a8-f85e99ea6919","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1945, which German city hosted the trials where former Nazi leaders were prosecuted for war crimes?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The proceedings became known as the Nuremberg Trials and helped establish that political and military leaders could be held individually responsible for international crimes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad31-70ce-8d0d-32bce4f76f75","description":"Nuremberg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7376-a31f-b4853e7170e5","description":"Berlin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7a13-a552-0f8d0c5ab1a0","description":"Munich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7b55-aca6-f1b635e179b4","description":"Frankfurt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad31-7504-8c81-920c8775c4e9","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the term used for a pirate who was licensed by the crown to capture enemy ships and cargo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A privateer operated under a letter of marque, making attacks on enemy vessels lawful for the crown; pirates acted without that authorization.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-a